## 4. Summary of evidence file:line

| Construct | Compiler support | Runtime support | Key files |
|---|---|---|---|
| `parallel_map` lowering | Full parse + metadata preservation | **None** (only static width) | `source_compiler.py:5326-5359`, `routing.py:59-63,302-309`, `manifest_backend.py:72-84,116-120` |
| Dynamic fanout | `FanoutPolicy(mode="dynamic")` preserved | Not consumed | `routing.py:59-63` |
| Suspension routes | `SuspensionRoute` in `WorkflowPolicy` | Basic detect, no auto-resume | `source_compiler.py:5647-5697`, `manifest_backend.py:324-332` |
| Loop policies | `LoopPolicy` on steps, backedge routes | Iteration counting + reentry | `source_compiler.py:4991-5053`, `routing.py:422-442` |
| Typed loop exits | Not evidenced | Not evidenced | — |

---

## 5. Specific amendment needed

If S2–S5 extraction sprints need end-to-end working dynamic fanout, **add a predecessor compiler-feature task** to implement dynamic `items_ref` resolution in the neutral router (`arnold/execution/routing.py`). The router currently gates on `_fanout_width`; it must also handle `mode="dynamic"` by resolving the `items_ref` from state (or delegating to a backend hook) and spawning children accordingly. Without this, `parallel_map` nodes in the compiled manifest are no-ops at runtime — the metadata is present but inert.

For typed loop exits, if the semantic parity plan requires the loop to produce a typed value consumed by downstream nodes, that is also unproven and would require a compiler + router feature task.
